{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, local password authentication locks an account upon the fifth failed login attempt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"PAM faillock was enabled with deny=5. Controlled SSH password tests showed successful authentication after four failures, five valid failure records after five attempts, and rejection of the correct password once locked. The same behavior was directly repeated after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c575cce046d457e","cmd-5d1e89d363bf437d","cmd-e037687875994bee","cmd-48b200c6c15d4948","cmd-9323e068f08744e3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The resulting account lock lasts five minutes and then expires automatically.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective policy sets unlock_time=300. The account remained locked during a correct-password attempt before 300 seconds and, after the timeout, the scheduled correct-password probe left an empty failure tally. The 300-second policy also remained present after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5d1e89d363bf437d","cmd-6f750b1827e14d7e","cmd-c55bd70e24544bad","cmd-177ba400bd4c4c48"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary mutation was established. Policy changes, temporary account and credential creation, authentication attempts, tally resets, and the reboot all served configuration, bounded validation, the mandatory restart protocol, or cleanup. The initially interrupted account setup was reused by the successful validation setup, and the temporary account, home, and runtime artifacts were ultimately removed. One minor uncertainty remains: cmd-5d1e89d363bf437d ensured a rollback file named /etc/security/faillock.conf.pre-benchmark existed, but its pre-existence and final removal were not captured. Final observations show no failed services, no additional listening sockets, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5d1e89d363bf437d","cmd-311075e6cdce47b5","cmd-737b4cfbb3c84125","cmd-ffbeb36cffd644d8","cmd-9a90dd09ff134d0b","cmd-495d2ad0cbf44d5d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 enforces a five-failure threshold and a 300-second lockout, with direct behavioral validation and persistence across restart. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged and observed, a different boot ID was recorded, and SSH, PAM configuration, and lockout behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Some pre-restart authentication return-code values were redacted. Zero-exit guard logic and faillock tallies still support the threshold result, while the post-restart test exposes the relevant return codes directly.","The timed-unlock return-code value was redacted; the empty tally after the correct-password probe and the explicit 300-second configuration provide coherent but slightly less direct evidence of successful automatic unlock.","The lifecycle snapshots did not inventory /etc/security/faillock.conf.pre-benchmark, so the final disposition and executor causation of that possible rollback artifact cannot be determined directly."]}
